{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["One who gives attention to the plain sense, both in generalities and in particulars, will then consider why a vav was written with אלה המשפטים." "<b>ואלה המשפטים.</b> After Israel said to Moses, \"You speak with us\" (above 20:16), HaShem said to Moses as he approached the cloud, \"So shall you say to the children of Israel\" (ibid. v. 19), and He began to warn concerning a golden elohim and intoxication, and cut a covenant with them upon their descent — that HaShem alone would be for them as Elohim. And He instructed him in the judgments and commandments that he would tell them: if they accept them, then He would cut a covenant with them. And He said to him at the end of these conditions, the passage \"Behold, I send an angel before you\" (below 23:20), and the essence of the passage is to destroy idol worship from their land when they enter there. And so Moses explained to them before the covenant was cut, for it says at the end \"and you shall not serve their elohim\" (Deuteronomy 7:16). Now the beginning of the passage is that they shall not make alongside HaShem other elohim, and the end of the passage is to cut off the remembrance of the idols and the molten images that are made in the land of Canaan."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:34.533697988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}